I Only Rendered This Because You Asked Me To.

Ingrid, the proud director who absolutely did not spend all night making this pretty for you.
Astrid, the horizontal coordinate who only walks beside you because you would get lost.
Sigrid, the vertical coordinate who saved you a seat but insists it was an accident.
Solveig, the quarter-unit depth who will look closer but only because your eyesight is hopeless.
Nora, the keeper of choices who remembered your favourite solid for no particular reason.
Liv, the voice of each glyph who is certainly not blushing when you read her lines.
Eira, the radial distance who measured the ring but says you must not get the wrong idea.
Frida, the first rotated coordinate who turns away whenever you catch her smiling.
Maja, the second rotated coordinate who fixed your angle because it was embarrassing.
Thea, the third rotated coordinate who looks back just to check you are keeping up.
Hedda, the ring distance who keeps her distance unless you look lonely.
Sunniva, the temporary depth who brought an extra scarf but claims she just hates waste.
Runa, the first normal who points toward the light and tells you to stop staring.
Tuva, the second normal who will hold your place but only this once.
Hanne, the third normal who shields your eyes and calls you a hopeless fool.
Vilde, the brightness who shines for the geometry and certainly not for your approval.

Act I: It is not as though I wanted to illuminate your world.

